1. wait()
Parent waits for any child process to finish.
Used to synchronize parent and child processes.
Prevents child from becoming a zombie after termination.
2. waitpid()
Parent waits for a specific child process.
Gives more control than wait().
3. Zombie Process
A child finishes execution, but its parent has not collected its exit status.
The child remains in the process table as a zombie.
wait() / waitpid() can remove the zombie.
4. Process Table
Stores information about processes.
A zombie remains in the process table until the parent collects its status.
